On the short end, high glycemic index foods measurably impair working memory and executive function for hours during the spike-crash cycle. But there's a subtler thing: glucose variability — the spike and crash pattern — appears more damaging than consistently elevated glucose. Your Saturday bomb may be worse than eating moderate carbs every day, because the metabolic whiplash is extreme.

